cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, cite the software and the associated manuscript."
title: "Leakage-Safe Cross-Domain Benchmarking for Bearing Fault Diagnosis: Time-Frequency Fusion, Calibration, and Self-Training"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lin"
    given-names: "Huadong"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ddlinSpark/leakage-safe-bearing-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/ddlinSpark/leakage-safe-bearing-benchmark"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - bearing fault diagnosis
  - domain generalization
  - data leakage
  - time-frequency learning
  - self-training
  - calibration
abstract: >-
  Reproducible code and derived results for a leakage-safe Paderborn bearing
  fault diagnosis benchmark using simultaneous unseen-bearing and
  unseen-operating-condition holdout, same-protocol external adaptations,
  fold-aware statistical analysis, raw-signal diagnostics, preprocessing and
  label-granularity sensitivity, calibration, and self-training audits.
